StudioTestRun.description:
One test run, as Studio knows it.

``id`` is the Studio ``test_run.id`` and is what ``{run_id}`` names in the route —
**never the platform id**, which is ``platform_run_id`` and is never accepted as a
locator. ``status`` is Studio's knowledge of the *dispatch*:

* ``pending`` — dispatch or reconciliation has not reached a fenced conclusion;
* ``started`` — Studio knows exactly one platform id; ``platform`` is live;
* ``failed_to_start`` — Studio has **proof** no dispatch was accepted;
* ``unknown`` — correlation completed but could not prove exactly one run;
* ``abandoned`` — recovery exhausted its attempt budget.

A non-null ``platform_run_id`` is an **invariant of** ``started``, not a partial
fact attached to another status. The four non-started states carry
``platform: null`` and cost no platform call.
